From: ashhart <71890694+ashhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:03:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] server: the reasoning split ends at the model's close token

The reply's reasoning was split at the first spelling of the close marker in the decoded
text, so a reply that quotes </think> while reasoning ended its reasoning at the quote and
the real answer after the model's own close token landed in the content. The server already
split at the close token's id for logprobs' answerStart and reasoning_tokens' count, and
those two agreed with each other and not with the text split.

The close marker is now found in the reply's tokens when it is one token, and the split
happens where that token's bytes begin. The stream and the whole reply both use it, and
every family with a reasoning split is covered, because the token id comes from the model
in use. The text split is kept for a tokenizer that has no token for the marker, and the
split falls back to "all reasoning" when the bytes at the offset are not the marker.

zig/src/server/think_split_test.zig is a server test over the real chat route: the reply
quotes the tag in three pieces, so the decoded text spells it exactly as the old split
looked for it, and the close token comes later. The reasoning keeps the quoted tag and the
answer follows the close token, whole and streamed.

(cherry picked from commit 23b943cb59a0f2129923dfd65768ad9803bdbbe4)
